" Spec [Chords][[Editing]]: <Ctrl-A>/<Ctrl-X> (songwriter#chord#TransposeChord)
" transpose the chord under the cursor by their count of semitones; off a chord
" they are Vim's own increment/decrement.

Given (transpose chord up chromatically):
               Am7

Execute (transpose chord up chromatically):
  call cursor(1, 14)
  call songwriter#chord#TransposeChord(1)
Expect:
               A#m7

Given (transpose chord down chromatically):
               Am7

Execute (transpose chord down chromatically):
  call cursor(1, 14)
  call songwriter#chord#TransposeChord(-1)
Expect:
               G#m7

Given (transpose chord wraps B -> C):
  Bm

Execute (transpose chord wraps B -> C):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#chord#TransposeChord(1)
Expect:
  Cm

Given (transpose chord wraps C -> B (down)):
  C

Execute (transpose chord wraps C -> B (down)):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#chord#TransposeChord(-1)
Expect:
  B

Given (transpose chord with sharp root):
  C#maj7

Execute (transpose chord with sharp root):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#chord#TransposeChord(1)
Expect:
  Dmaj7

Given (no-op on non-chord text):
  hello world

Execute (no-op on non-chord text):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#chord#TransposeChord(1)
Expect:
  hello world

Given (a word starting with a chord letter is not a chord):
  Bad

Execute (a word starting with a chord letter is not a chord):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#chord#TransposeChord(1)
Expect:
  Bad

Given (a chord root must start the token):
  xAm

Execute (a chord root must start the token):
  call cursor(1, 2)
  call songwriter#chord#TransposeChord(1)
Expect:
  xAm

Given (a slash chord transposes as a whole, with the cursor on the bass):
  D/F#

Execute (a slash chord transposes as a whole, with the cursor on the bass):
  call cursor(1, 3)
  call songwriter#chord#TransposeChord(1)
Expect:
  D#/G

Given (TransposeChord moves by the given number of semitones):
  Am

Execute (TransposeChord moves by the given number of semitones):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#chord#TransposeChord(-3)
Expect:
  F#m

Given songwriter (<C-A> on a number off a chord is native increment):
  verse 2

Execute (<C-A> on a number off a chord is native increment):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  execute "normal \<C-A>"
Expect:
  verse 3

Given songwriter (<C-X> with a count is native decrement off a chord):
  repeat x10

Execute (<C-X> with a count is native decrement off a chord):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  execute "normal 4\<C-X>"
Expect:
  repeat x6

Given songwriter (<C-A> with a count transposes a chord by that many semitones):
  Am

Execute (<C-A> with a count transposes a chord by that many semitones):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  execute "normal 2\<C-A>"
Expect:
  Bm

Given songwriter (<C-A> on a tab line increments the next fret, not the string name):
  B|--3--|

Execute (<C-A> on a tab line increments the next fret, not the string name):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  execute "normal \<C-A>"
Expect:
  B|--4--|
